# BLU-000 — Blueprint title

> **Summary:** The future-state design and the gap it closes.
> **Epistemic:** Which designs exist and which problem each attacks.
> **Pragmatic:** Consult when designing something new.
> **Audience:** Agents · Oracles

> **A blueprint is a design not yet executed** (STD-001 §2). It is not a
> report of what happened.

---

## Current state

What exists today, and where the gap is. The measured or named defect that
makes this blueprint necessary.

## Future state

The architecture after execution. Concrete: components, connections,
boundaries, data flows.

## The gap

What separates current from future state, and why it has not been closed
already (cost, risk, dependency).

